From c35cc72e725450d5df75c9ba37880f4856c012ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@example.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 11:29:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Consumption per km: sum over periods instead of discarding
 short intervals

The old per-interval filter (kWh > 0 and km >= 20) threw away a short interval
together with the energy in its window, but that energy belonged to the drive
before it, whose km were already counted. With a daily plug-in after short trips
it showed 15.3 kWh/100 km for a car that really uses 18.0.

- EfficiencyCalc (pure, 40 checks): km from the odometer at plug-in, kWh from the
  charges that refilled it, summed per period before dividing; month and rolling
  30/90/365-day figures; confidence level with reason; unpriced charges estimated
- Date range = the drives that END in it (no lost boundary interval)
- A single bad odometer reading (sensor reports 0 once) is rejected instead of
  inflating the next interval; a real reset is kept
- Card shows 30/90 days, selected period and a month table per vehicle; charges
  without a vehicle are reported; the cumulative charts are kept
- Verified on two cars with known efficiency (18.0 / 12.0): new 17.7 / 11.7, old
  15.3 / 11.8; the page was run in jsdom against the PHP server
